Subject: [PATCH] eth_stm32: recover ETH ISR device from DT under USERSPACE

On stm32f746 with CONFIG_USERSPACE the generated _sw_isr_table argument
for the ETH IRQ is written 8 bytes below the real device object, so
eth_isr()'s dev->data reads the device's api pointer (a flash const)
instead of dev_data; the ensuing k_sem_give() faults in sys_dlist_remove
on the first TX-complete IRQ. Recover the instance from the DT symbol.

diff --git a/drivers/ethernet/eth_stm32_hal_common.c b/drivers/ethernet/eth_stm32_hal_common.c
index be97dfac15f..482cb9b0757 100644
--- a/drivers/ethernet/eth_stm32_hal_common.c
+++ b/drivers/ethernet/eth_stm32_hal_common.c
@@ -88,6 +88,18 @@ static void rx_thread(void *arg1, void *unused1, void *unused2)
 
 static void eth_isr(const struct device *dev)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Under CONFIG_USERSPACE the generated _sw_isr_table argument for the
+	 * ETH IRQ lands 8 bytes below the real device object (device symbol
+	 * minus 8), so the incoming `dev` points into the previous device and
+	 * `dev->data` reads the wrong field (the device's `api` pointer, a flash
+	 * const) instead of the real dev_data. A subsequent k_sem_give() then
+	 * walks a garbage wait/poll list and faults in sys_dlist_remove. Recover
+	 * the correct instance straight from the devicetree symbol (a direct
+	 * .text relocation, not routed through the corrupted ISR table); this is
+	 * a no-op for the non-USERSPACE build. Single ETH instance on this SoC.
+	 */
+	dev = DEVICE_DT_INST_GET(0);
 	struct eth_stm32_hal_dev_data *dev_data = dev->data;
 	ETH_HandleTypeDef *heth = &dev_data->heth;
 
